---
import { ISSUES_URL, REPO_URL } from "../lib/links";
---

<section class="border-t border-line">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Open source, MIT-licensed</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-muted">
      Every line of code and every design decision is public. Use it, fork it, host it yourself.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-8 space-y-3">
      <li>
        <span class="text-muted">→</span> Try it on your machine and{" "}
        <a href={ISSUES_URL} class="underline underline-offset-4">report</a> anything that cuts wrong
        or is confusing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-muted">→</span> Add your router to the machine presets, with a source for
        every value.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-muted">→</span> Read and discuss the product requirements and architecture
        decisions on{" "}<a href={REPO_URL} class="underline underline-offset-4">GitHub</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
